     "text": "{\"score\": 6.5, \"grade\": \"B\", \"reason\": \"The signal bar opened at roughly 115 (a 13% gap from the prior close of ~101.71) and the entire bar range is only 7.8% of price, meaning the gap accounts for the overwhelming majority of the 17.46% move — the actual intraday range expansion is modest and the burst is gap-dominated rather than a genuine intraday thrust. A 17.46% gain on a biotech name with a 13.1% gap is the textbook apparent-catalyst pattern (likely an earnings or data release), which is an Episodic Pivot setup with a different plan, not a clean momentum burst out of a quiet base. The base itself looks orderly in the shaded region, but the signal bar's gap-dominated structure and the biotech catalyst flag materially reduce the quality of this as a reaction entry.\", \"key_risk\": \"The 17.46% gap-driven burst on a biotech flag almost certainly reflects a catalyst event; the after-close entry plan is designed for momentum continuation, not post-catalyst digestion, and the 36% win rate noted for 15%+ gains compounds this risk.\", \"findings\": [{\"criterion\": \"signal_shape\", \"source\": \"strategy.chart.signal\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"burst.gap_pct\", \"value\": 13.1}, {\"path\": \"burst.bar_range_pct\", \"value\": 7.8}, {\"path\": \"burst.gain_pct\", \"value\": 17.46}], \"observation\": \"gap_dominated\"}, {\"criterion\": \"event_structure\", \"source\": \"strategy.chart.event\", \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"burst.gap_pct\", \"value\": 13.1}, {\"path\": \"burst.volume_vs_avg50\", \"value\": 3.94}, {\"path\": \"burst.volume_rank_60\", \"value\": 1}], \"observation\": \"apparent_catalyst_gap\"}], \"entry_note\": \"Skip if the open gaps further above 119.47 or if the stock opens below the signal day's close, as either would confirm post-catalyst exhaustion rather than orderly continuation.\"}",
